Do you know how much money?

705
00:29:39,569 --> 00:29:43,782
I'm close to a 100,000 dollars 
spent on the Hillside property right now.

706
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:47,994
[Jason] We split the marketing costs
with the agent, but we front those costs

707
00:29:48,077 --> 00:29:51,331
and we get reimbursed when the property 
sells and the agent make a commission.

708
00:29:51,414 --> 00:29:54,250
So if the agent doesn't make a commission
because the property doesn't sell,

709
00:29:54,334 --> 00:29:55,919
we're stuck with the marketing costs.

710
00:29:56,002 --> 00:29:58,505
-All we need is one client, you know? One.
-No.

711
00:29:58,588 --> 00:30:01,591
-Could be an international buyer...
-Now you sound like an unrealistic seller.

712
00:30:01,674 --> 00:30:03,760
-"Oh, we just need one client."
-But we do.

713
00:30:03,843 --> 00:30:07,263
That's almost embarrassing for us
to list it that high.

714
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:08,807
I don't think it's embarrassing.

715
00:30:08,890 --> 00:30:11,267
What if we sat on the market for months
and got no showings?

716
00:30:11,351 --> 00:30:13,353
-I agree with you.
-He's gonna think it's our fault.

717
00:30:13,436 --> 00:30:15,271
Am I really not gonna try? Like...

718
00:30:15,605 --> 00:30:17,565
That's like life-changing to me, you know?

719
00:30:17,649 --> 00:30:21,277
But I'm more concerned that you're going
to just waste money. What about...

720
00:30:22,153 --> 00:30:23,738
49 million?

721
00:30:23,822 --> 00:30:25,073
[inhales sharply] I mean--

722
00:30:25,156 --> 00:30:26,991
That's, like, a price I think 
we can get behind.

723
00:30:27,075 --> 00:30:30,370
But my point is, someone might offer 65.

724
00:30:30,453 --> 00:30:33,164
-No one's offering 65.
-[Davina] How do you know?

725
00:30:33,248 --> 00:30:35,500
-Because I know.
-Why can't I just try?

726
00:30:35,583 --> 00:30:36,751
'Cause it's not a good look
for the brokerage.

727
00:30:36,834 --> 00:30:38,378
What am I supposed to tell him?

728
00:30:38,461 --> 00:30:40,421
"It's embarrassing?
Jason thinks it's embarrassing"?

729
00:30:40,505 --> 00:30:41,589
I can't say that to the client.

730
00:30:41,673 --> 00:30:44,217
It's a detriment to us
and it's a detriment to him.

731
00:30:44,300 --> 00:30:46,344
He's gotta understand 
it's not good for him either.

732
00:30:46,427 --> 00:30:48,638
-Listen, Davina--
-I think you're being negative.

733
00:30:48,721 --> 00:30:50,807
[Davina] It seems like Jason won't budge.
It's frustrating.

734
00:30:50,890 --> 00:30:53,434
I mean, if I worked for myself,
I could just take the listing

735
00:30:53,518 --> 00:30:54,936
and not have to worry about Jason.

736
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:55,853
How's this?

737
00:30:55,937 --> 00:30:59,774
I'll think about it, and you tell him
it's worth 50 million,

738
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:01,985
and that he needs to get more realistic.

739
00:31:02,068 --> 00:31:03,444
Otherwise, we're wasting his time.

740
00:31:03,528 --> 00:31:06,781
I'm going to respectfully show him
the comps

741
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:07,991
and tell him your recommendation.

742
00:31:08,074 --> 00:31:09,742
-Fine.
-And I'm gonna say let's talk about

743
00:31:09,826 --> 00:31:13,663
how to best market this property
and the list price.

744
00:31:13,746 --> 00:31:14,872
[Jason] Okay, fine.

745
00:31:14,956 --> 00:31:16,749
[Heather] Tarek's birthday
is on Wednesday,

746
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:19,127
so I got him a Tumi travel case.

747
00:31:19,669 --> 00:31:22,839
And he's obsessed with ChapStick
so I'm gonna get him a bunch of ChapStick.

748
00:31:22,922 --> 00:31:24,173
[Amanza] Isn't that cute?

749
00:31:24,257 --> 00:31:25,425
When's his birthday?

750
00:31:25,508 --> 00:31:26,968
-[Heather] Wednesday.
-Oh.

751
00:31:27,051 --> 00:31:28,428
[Heather] He's gonna be 38.

752
00:31:28,511 --> 00:31:29,971
I texted his ex this morning

753
00:31:30,054 --> 00:31:31,180
to touch base and...

754
00:31:31,264 --> 00:31:32,265
-[Christine] Who?
-His ex.

755
00:31:32,974 --> 00:31:33,975
[Heather] The ex-wife.

756
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:36,769
-[Christine] You have her number?
-He gave it to me to text her.

757
00:31:36,853 --> 00:31:37,729
Really?

758
00:31:38,354 --> 00:31:39,939
[Christine] Text her what?

759
00:31:40,023 --> 00:31:43,568
[Heather] Because I'm around the kids,
so I wanted to introduce myself.

760
00:31:44,152 --> 00:31:45,111
What?

761
00:31:48,948 --> 00:31:49,949
[Christine] I gotta...

762
00:31:50,033 --> 00:31:52,452
[Christine chuckles] I just had a moment.

763
00:31:52,535 --> 00:31:54,287
I mean, why wouldn't I?

764
00:31:54,370 --> 00:31:57,916
I'm just saying, as a mom,
as a person who went through it,

765
00:31:57,999 --> 00:31:59,626
-that's a good thing.
-Exactly.

766
00:31:59,709 --> 00:32:03,379
[Amanza] I haven't even met
my ex-husband's girlfriend.

767
00:32:03,463 --> 00:32:05,006
My kids live with her.

768
00:32:05,089 --> 00:32:07,926
And I'm like, I want--
We need to go to lunch.

769
00:32:08,009 --> 00:32:09,969
-Exactly.
-She's helping raise my children.

770
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:11,929
[Heather] That's exactly what I said
to Tarek last night.

771
00:32:12,013 --> 00:32:16,643
I will say though, it terrifies me
how fast you have met those kids.

772
00:32:17,018 --> 00:32:18,311
-Because--
-[Heather] Why?

773
00:32:18,394 --> 00:32:21,272
Because when and if something 
doesn't work out,

774
00:32:21,731 --> 00:32:25,109
-their hearts are crushed.
-Excuse me, when what doesn't work out?

775
00:32:25,318 --> 00:32:26,569
[Amanza] It can happen.

776
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:27,820
I said, "When or if."

777
00:32:28,279 --> 00:32:31,115
"When and if" is not gonna happen.
It's gonna work out.

778
00:32:31,199 --> 00:32:33,409
We are very serious and...

779
00:32:34,035 --> 00:32:35,244
going to move in together

780
00:32:35,328 --> 00:32:37,246
and we're like moving forward
with everything.

781
00:32:37,330 --> 00:32:39,082
So it's like.. I'd like to...

782
00:32:39,165 --> 00:32:42,543
[Amanza] That's all fine and dandy.
I'm saying, I hope that you guys work out,

783
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:45,213
because if you break up,
those children are crushed.

784
00:32:45,296 --> 00:32:47,465
I just went through it and it sucks.

785
00:32:47,548 --> 00:32:49,926
It's like the hardest,
most heart-breaking thing.

786
00:32:50,009 --> 00:32:52,512
I'm glad you're worried about
my boyfriend's children, thank you.

787
00:32:52,595 --> 00:32:53,972
[Christine laughing]

788
00:32:54,055 --> 00:32:54,931
[Heather] Thank you.

789
00:32:55,014 --> 00:32:56,766
-Listen--
-[Heather] No, I do too, though.

790
00:32:56,849 --> 00:32:59,727
If I thought you were going to be
this angry at me for saying it,

791
00:32:59,811 --> 00:33:01,020
I would've kept my mouth shut.

792
00:33:01,104 --> 00:33:03,314
-Good.
-I thought you knew me well enough to know

793
00:33:03,398 --> 00:33:06,442
that I'm, like, not intentionally 
bashing your relationship,

794
00:33:06,526 --> 00:33:07,777
saying that you're a bad person,

795
00:33:07,860 --> 00:33:11,072
saying that he's introduced 
his, you know, kids to everybody.

796
00:33:11,155 --> 00:33:15,243
I literally picked up on what you guys
were talking about and had a comment.

797
00:33:15,827 --> 00:33:19,455
So I didn't feel like that was gonna cause
this huge negative reaction.

798
00:33:20,456 --> 00:33:24,085
I care. I felt like sharing. Caring.

799
00:33:24,168 --> 00:33:26,087
Thank you for your opinion,
I appreciate that.

800
00:33:27,004 --> 00:33:29,507
Well, you don't.
Or else we wouldn't have had this...

801
00:33:29,590 --> 00:33:32,427
-I actually don't, but thank you anyways.
-[Amanza] Then don't say you do.

802
00:33:32,510 --> 00:33:34,512
That's... That's immature.

803
00:33:35,263 --> 00:33:36,097
[Heather] Okay.

804
00:33:36,848 --> 00:33:40,143
I just think people should mind 
their own business. [scoffs]

805
00:33:40,685 --> 00:33:46,607
♪ It's a good time
To let the madness play  ♪

806
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:48,359
♪ Dirty, dirty secret ♪

807
00:33:48,443 --> 00:33:52,947
♪ My pretty lie... ♪

808
00:33:55,283 --> 00:33:58,619
[Davina] It's always tough telling
a client their asking price is too high,

809
00:33:58,703 --> 00:33:59,871
but it's part of the job.

810
00:33:59,954 --> 00:34:01,998
So I just hope he can be reasonable.

811
00:34:03,916 --> 00:34:05,376
[doorbell rings]

812
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:06,294
[Ece] Davina.

813
00:34:06,377 --> 00:34:07,962
-Hi, how are you?
-Hi.

814
00:34:08,045 --> 00:34:10,840
-Great to see you.
-Thanks for having me.

815
00:34:11,257 --> 00:34:13,259
[Ece] Adnan is here in the living room.

816
00:34:13,926 --> 00:34:15,386
-Please, this way.
-Oh, great.

817
00:34:16,971 --> 00:34:18,973
[clicking fingers]

818
00:34:19,849 --> 00:34:20,808
Hi.

819
00:34:21,225 --> 00:34:22,560
-Hi, how are you?
-Great to see you.

820
00:34:22,643 --> 00:34:24,562
[Adnan] Welcome. Take a seat, please.

821
00:34:24,645 --> 00:34:26,397
So, how is life? How is everything?

822
00:34:26,481 --> 00:34:28,316
-It's good, it's good.
-Great.

823
00:34:28,399 --> 00:34:31,235
Just trying to put a lot 
of energy into work.

824
00:34:31,319 --> 00:34:35,364
So, I obviously want to talk to you
about your listing, this property.

825
00:34:35,782 --> 00:34:40,203
Um... I know we were talking
about sort of 80 million, the pricing...

826
00:34:40,286 --> 00:34:43,790
I talked to Jason,
the owner of my brokerage, and...

827
00:34:44,373 --> 00:34:47,251
he felt like 80 million 
was very high for the area.

828
00:34:48,419 --> 00:34:52,006
And he felt it was just kind
of a bit too aggressive.

829
00:34:52,381 --> 00:34:56,052
And... I know...
[nervous laugh] I understand.

830
00:34:56,135 --> 00:34:57,136
Um...

831
00:34:57,220 --> 00:34:59,514
[Davina laughs nervously]

832
00:34:59,597 --> 00:35:03,643
[laughing nervously]
So he, you know, he was telling me

833
00:35:03,726 --> 00:35:06,687
that he felt it'd make
the brokers look bad

834
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:08,898
if we came on at a very high price.

835
00:35:08,981 --> 00:35:12,777
He felt like he needed the pricing
to be at 60 million.

836
00:35:14,320 --> 00:35:16,531
I know, I don't agree with that.

837
00:35:16,614 --> 00:35:19,158
Um... I know that
that's not going to work. Um...

838
00:35:20,451 --> 00:35:23,287
So I don't know if you would consider
any kind of lower number 

839
00:35:23,371 --> 00:35:25,790
or if we can talk
about anything like that.

840
00:35:29,502 --> 00:35:31,504
Sixty is out of question.

841
00:35:31,587 --> 00:35:33,464
-Yeah...
-[Adnan] First of all, the realtors,

842
00:35:33,548 --> 00:35:36,592
they always get the same answer, right?
"Let's take the price down."

843
00:35:36,676 --> 00:35:38,427
-I understand.
-But really,

844
00:35:38,511 --> 00:35:40,179
you should increase the price, right?

845
00:35:40,263 --> 00:35:44,517
I mean it took years to build 
our reputation and image.

846
00:35:44,600 --> 00:35:45,476
Yeah.

847
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:49,605
We are not just building 
20,000 square-foot mansions.

848
00:35:50,314 --> 00:35:51,691
They are not cheap.

849
00:35:51,774 --> 00:35:53,192
Um...

850
00:35:53,276 --> 00:35:56,362
But I'm having to deal 
with Jason, my brokerage,

851
00:35:56,445 --> 00:35:59,073
who's not willing to take it over 60.

852
00:35:59,657 --> 00:36:00,616
So...

853
00:36:00,700 --> 00:36:04,162
Honey, you know that 
we have a lot of realtors...

854
00:36:04,245 --> 00:36:06,247
-Yeah, absolutely.
-...who we are in contact with

855
00:36:06,330 --> 00:36:08,374
as we are continuously building.

856
00:36:08,457 --> 00:36:11,294
You or Jason might want
to have something cheaper,

857
00:36:11,377 --> 00:36:13,421
there are lots of them on the market,

858
00:36:13,504 --> 00:36:15,548
but if you really want something good,

859
00:36:15,631 --> 00:36:16,799
that costs, baby.

860
00:36:16,883 --> 00:36:18,801
No, I'm very well aware. I mean,

861
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:24,140
I think it does command more than 50,
60 million, of the properties in the area.

862
00:36:24,223 --> 00:36:26,392
I think we can go 70 maybe, but...

863
00:36:26,475 --> 00:36:28,477
Honey, I don't like you 
negotiating with me.

864
00:36:28,561 --> 00:36:30,938
You should be negotiating
with the clients, not with me.

865
00:36:31,022 --> 00:36:33,524
-Absolutely. Yes, sir.
-You should be getting the best price.

866
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:35,568
Um...

867
00:36:36,944 --> 00:36:38,696
This is a huge opportunity for me.

868
00:36:38,779 --> 00:36:41,824
It's the most expensive listing 
I would ever have.

869
00:36:41,908 --> 00:36:44,202
And I'm so grateful
that you're considering me.

870
00:36:44,285 --> 00:36:45,620
You know, I have clients and contacts 

871
00:36:45,703 --> 00:36:49,165
and other agents that I know
that may have buyers for this.

872
00:36:49,749 --> 00:36:55,296
So... I think I could generate a buyer
closer to 80 as an offer.

873
00:37:03,179 --> 00:37:05,765
Fine. We will work with you,

874
00:37:06,223 --> 00:37:08,976
but I want you to perform.

875
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:11,103
I don't want only fancy words

876
00:37:11,187 --> 00:37:12,980
-and all this stuff.
-I understand.

877
00:37:13,064 --> 00:37:15,608
And we'll make a deal
with you for three months.

878
00:37:15,691 --> 00:37:17,902
-Okay.
-Only three months this project.

879
00:37:18,527 --> 00:37:21,948
Okay, so let her have that for 75.

880
00:37:22,031 --> 00:37:24,367
[Davina] Okay. Thank you so much Adnan, 
I appreciate it.

881
00:37:24,450 --> 00:37:25,534
[Adnan] Congratulations.

882
00:37:25,618 --> 00:37:27,620
I'm not going to let you down.
Thank you very much.

